    {
      "text": "Bangladesh's National Adaptation Plan (NAP) estimates that nearly US$230 billion (approximately Tk 28.52 trillion) will be required by 2050 to address climate challenges. However, the climate-related allocation for 25 ministries and divisions for the 2026–27 fiscal year is set at Tk 517.46 billion. Of that amount, the government-financed Climate Change Trust Fund has received Tk 1 billion. Additionally, a large portion of international public climate finance is provided in the form of loans."
    },
    {
      "text": "In Sirajganj town, a solar-powered water pump installed two years ago through a local NGO initiative funded by a climate fund serves a slum in Amlapara. Residents, including Maksuda Begum and Rahela Khatun, reported that the pump has reduced difficulties in accessing water compared to the previous municipal supply line. While the project has impacted the Amlapara slum, local residents and municipal officials state that there are approximately 30 slums in the town and no other slum currently has a similar facility."
    }
  ]
}

